    "changelog": [
      "Core Principles: emphasised that cuts must never split single orthographic/lexical units (compounds, names, numeral+counter sequences, open quotes) and clarified that such positions are not acceptable candidates.",
      "When to Segment: strengthened surface cues delaying high confidence (wait for clause-final predicate, negation, counter, closing quote) and listed more explicit indicators that the preceding text still needs disambiguation.",
      "Never Segment: added absolute prohibitions for cutting inside continuous lexical units, between numeral and counter, inside open quotes, and immediately after name-internal delimiter; made the list explicit and concise so implementers never propose these positions.",
      "Priority Rules: demoted early-in-sentence and comma-adjacent cuts more strongly, and required explicit disambiguators (predicate ending, counter, closing quote, negation) before a candidate can be given high confidence.",
      "Decision Procedure: tightened the two-step workflow with an explicit automatic-demotion/removal step for candidates that would split tokens or precede imminent disambiguators, and required promotion to high ranks only when a safe disambiguator or sealed clause is present."
    ],
    "next_changelog": [
      "Core Principles: strengthened the 'avoid premature commitment' rule to explicitly delay finalizing noun phrases, prenominal/genitive modifiers, enumerations, subject-only fragments (～が), adverbials, temporal/scope modifiers, verb clusters, agent/person/tense assignments and polarity until disambiguating heads/predicates/counters/negators/list-closers appear.",
      "When to Segment: merged measured candidate rules into the disambiguator list and added explicit surface indicators to flag prenominal modifiers, incomplete enumerations, subject-only fragments, temporal/adverbial modifiers, and verb-cluster splits as risky (lower confidence) positions unless a clear disambiguator has already appeared.",
      "Priority Rules: consolidated multiple candidate_rules into the demotions/special cautions: strongly demote (but do not forbid) cuts that would finalize quantity/extent before counters/quantifiers, separate modifiers from their heads, split enumerations or name lists, assert existence/polarity from a subject-only fragment, or break verb-complement chains; prefer promoting only when a clear disambiguator or sealed clause is present.",
      "Decision Procedure: added explicit candidate-flagging for trailing prenominal modifiers, incomplete name/enumeration lists, subject-only ～が fragments, temporal/adverbial modifiers, and verb-cluster/object splits; require these flagged candidates to be demoted unless an explicit disambiguator (predicate/negation, counter, case particle completing a noun, closing quote, or list-close token) is already present before promotion to high confidence."
    ]
